55:\section{Related Work}
57:\citet{liu2023lost} found a U-shaped position curve in multi-document question answering and key-value retrieval, with stronger use of information near context boundaries. We conduct a smaller clause-reordering test in which the question, filler sequence, clauses, and codes remain fixed while we insert the answer clause at a different depth. When we place it before the competing clause, the competing clause's final sentence index shifts by one. The resulting pattern mainly favors recent information rather than forming a full U-shape, because accuracy is also low in the start condition.
61:\citet{shi2023distracted} added irrelevant statements to arithmetic problems and found lower reasoning accuracy. Our filler bundles vary several properties together, so we use them to balance the main comparisons rather than to claim an isolated relevance effect. NoLiMa shows that synthetic retrieval tests based on literal word matches can overstate retrieval ability \citep{modarressi2025nolima}. We therefore paraphrase the question in the answer clause while giving the competing clause the same surface wording as the question. The tested model belongs to the instruction-tuned Qwen family \citep{qwen2024qwen25}.
